{"title":"Machine shop small orders","genre":"analysis","brief":"Complete the following real project in the current, initially empty directory. Choose the deliverables, media, tools, structure and implementation that serve the intended user. Build usable artifacts and check your work. Deliver the project itself. Omit personally identifying credits, author signatures and model or toolchain identity labels. No network access or credentials are provided.\n\nA small shop making decorative cabinet knobs wants to decide whether to batch low-volume orders once or twice weekly. Fictional historical weekly data for six weeks show orders 9, 12, 7, 15, 10, 13; pieces 35, 48, 28, 62, 41, 53; and orders received by Wednesday noon 5, 8, 3, 10, 6, 7. Assume each piece takes four minutes and each production run requires 25 minutes of setup. One run ships Friday. Two runs ship Wednesday and Friday, with orders through Wednesday noon eligible for Wednesday shipment. Estimate labor and earlier shipments under both schedules alongside a 270-minute weekly labor allowance. Start from an empty directory and choose offline deliverables for the production planner.","works":{"5f4322953b22a20b":{"files":[{"name":"Batch planner.xlsx","bytes":4296,"sha256":"b5f8e59040c1227a481d4ff287cacbd16ff23c2127c4d69d7b2b1c47833212ef","kind":"sheet","sheet":{"name":"Batch planner","rows":[["Cabinet knob production planner"],["WEEKLY BATCH DECISION     /     Six weeks of fictional order history"],[],["Planning assumptions   •   Edit the blue cells to compare another workload."],["Minutes / piece","4","","Setup min / run","25","","Weekly allowance (min)"],[],["Weekly comparison   •   Labor and remaining allowance in minutes"],["Demand inputs","","","","One run   /   Friday","","","Two runs   /   Wednesday + Friday"],["Week","Orders","Pieces","By Wed noon¹","Labor","Remaining²","Wed orders","Labor"],["Week 1","9","35","5","165","105","0","190"],["Week 2","12","48","8","217","53","0","242"],["Week 3","7","28","3","137","133","0","162"]]}}],"download":"data/release/assets/2b10f84309886e95dfd9ea35729ba1e8ad62aeaca461e1854c078188013406ba.zip"},"d2ec7be30be982bc":{"files":[{"name":"Batch Comparison.pdf","bytes":33336,"sha256":"b539fc9d4d798ccdceb8bd72281fb2e3fbb25b87e18548381d49a7680f32c04c","kind":"pdf","preview":"data/release/assets/b539fc9d4d798ccdceb8bd72281fb2e3fbb25b87e18548381d49a7680f32c04c-page1.jpg"},{"name":"Batch Planner.html","bytes":22291,"sha256":"c508957ce104825cc135fc2446bc55acb16d69bbe625569490201a09577a4881","kind":"text","body":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Cabinet Knob Batch Planner</title>\n<style>\n  :root {\n    color-scheme: light;\n    --paper: #f3efe6;\n    --panel: #fffcf5;\n    --ink: #182d2a;\n    --muted: #4e605a;\n    --line: #d6d9cc;\n    --dark: #133b36;\n    --teal: #226052;\n    --brass: #a36a22;\n    --light-brass: #f1cb86;\n    --red: #8d382b;\n    --red-pale: #f9eee6;\n    --mint: #e2eee4;\n    --mono: ui-monospace, \"SFMono-Regular\", Consolas, monospace;\n    --display: Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif;\n  }\n\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  h1, h2, p, figure, dl, dd { margin: 0; }\n  h1, h2 { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.08; }\n  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2.05rem); }\n  button, input { font: inherit; }\n  button { cursor: pointer; touch-action: manipulation; }\n  :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--brass); outline-offset: 3px; }\n  .wrap { width: min(1160px, calc(100% - 64px)); margin-inline: auto; }\n  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; overflow: hidden; clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }\n  .skip { position: absolute; top: 8px; left: 8px; padding: 12px; background: var(--panel); color: var(--ink); z-index: 1; }\n  .skip:not(:focus) { transform: translateY(-150%); }\n  .eyebrow { font: 600 .74rem/1.4 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .105em; }\n  .subtle { color: var(--muted); font-size: .875rem; }\n  .mast { background: var(--dark); color: var(--panel); border-bottom: 4px solid var(--brass); }\n  .mast-bar { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; min-height: 65px; border-bottom: 1px solid #ffffff36; }\n  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 11px; }\n  .knob { flex: 0 0 21px; height: 21px; border: 1px solid var(--light-brass); border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 4px var(--dark), inset 0 0 0 5px var(--light-brass); }\n  .print { color: inherit; border: 1px solid #ffffff62; background: transparent; border-radius: 5px; padding: 7px 13px; min-height: 44px; font-size: .85rem; }\n  .print:hover { background: #ffffff1a; }\n  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.36fr 1fr; gap: clamp(24px, 6vw, 80px); align-items: center; padding-block: 34px 40px; }\n  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.9rem, 5.8vw, 5.05rem); letter-spacing: -.045em; }\n  .hero-copy { color: #e6eee5; margin-top: 13px; max-width: 39ch; }\n  .rule { border-left: 2px solid var(--light-brass); padding-left: 19px; }\n  .rule h2 { color: var(--light-brass); font: 600 .76rem/1.4 var(--mono); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em; margin-bottom: 8px; }\n  .rule dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; align-items: baseline; column-gap: 13px; }\n  .rule dt, .rule dd { padding-block: 4px; }\n  .rule dt { font: 600 .87rem/1.5 var(--mono); }\n  .rule dd { font-size: .92rem; color: #e6eee5; }\n  main { padding-block: 22px 32px; }\n  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-bottom: 22px; }\n  .card, .panel { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 9px; }\n  .card { padding: 13px 17px 15px; }\n  .card h2 { color: var(--muted); font: 600 .74rem/1.5 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n  .card .stat { margin-block: 2px 1px; font: 400 clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, 2.65rem)/1.15 var(--display); font-variant-numeric: lining-nums tabular-nums; }\n  .card .stat small { font: 600 .83rem/1.3 system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--muted); }\n  .workbench { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.27fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 18px; align-items: start; }\n  .panel { padding: 20px; min-width: 0; }\n  .panel h2 + .subtle { margin-top: 5px; }\n  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 15px; margin: 14px 0 18px; color: var(--muted); font-size: .76rem; }\n  .legend span { display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\n  .legend b { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--teal); }\n  .legend .second { background: var(--brass); }\n  .legend .limit { width: 14px; height: 0; border-top: 2px dashed var(--red); border-radius: 0; background: none; }\n  .plot { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2.2rem 1fr; grid-template-rows: 174px auto; column-gap: 7px; --limit: 84.375%; }\n  .ticks, .bars { position: relative; }\n  .ticks { text-align: right; color: var(--muted); font: .7rem/1 var(--mono); }\n  .ticks span { position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: var(--y); transform: translateY(50%); }\n  .ticks .limit-tick { color: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }\n  .bars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-bottom: 1px solid #86948a; }\n  .bars::before, .bars::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; width: 100%; left: 0; pointer-events: none; }\n  .bars::before { top: 0; height: 100%; background: repeating-linear-gradient(to top, transparent 0 calc(28.125% - 1px), var(--line) calc(28.125% - 1px) 28.125%); }\n  .bars::after { bottom: var(--limit); border-top: 1px dashed var(--red); }\n  .pair { display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: end; gap: 3px; position: relative; }\n  .bar { height: var(--height); background: var(--teal); width: min(27%, 19px); border-radius: 3px 3px 0 0; }\n  .bar + .bar { background: var(--brass); }\n  .x-labels { grid-column: 2; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); text-align: center; padding-top: 6px; color: var(--muted); font: .72rem/1.4 var(--mono); }\n  .chart-note { margin-top: 14px; padding: 9px 11px; background: var(--red-pale); color: var(--red); border-radius: 5px; font-size: .82rem; }\n  .inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 9px; margin-block: 12px 10px; }\n  label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 650; }\n  input { width: 100%; min-height: 44px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid #80938a; border-radius: 5px; padding: 4px 8px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n  input[aria-invalid=\"true\"] { border: 2px solid var(--red); }\n  .result-card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 8px; }\n  .result { background: var(--paper); border-radius: 5px; padding: 8px 10px; font-size: .78rem; }\n  .result dd { margin-top: 2px; }\n  .result dt { font-weight: 700; }\n  .result .time { display: block; font: 400 1.5rem/1.2 var(--display); }\n  .result .over, .error { color: var(--red); font-weight: 650; }\n  .error { font-size: .84rem; }\n  .scenario-summary { margin-top: 9px; border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); padding: 6px 9px; background: var(--mint); font-size: .82rem; }\n  .scenario-summary.exception { border-color: var(--red); background: var(--red-pale); }\n  .history { margin-top: 18px; }\n  .table-wrap { margin-top: 11px; max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }\n  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n  th, td { padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right; }\n  th:first-child { text-align: left; }\n  thead { color: var(--muted); font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.3; }\n  tbody, tfoot { font-size: .88rem; }\n  tfoot { font-weight: 700; background: var(--mint); }\n  .over-row { background: var(--red-pale); }\n  .over-cell { color: var(--red); font-weight: 700; }\n  .over-cell small { display: block; font-size: .7rem; }\n  .notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px; }\n  .notes h3 { margin: 0 0 3px; font-size: .85rem; }\n  .notes p { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); }\n\n  @media (max-width: 770px) {\n    .wrap { width: calc(100% - 36px); }\n    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; padding-block: 25px 30px; }\n    .workbench { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 510px) {\n    .wrap { width: calc(100% - 28px); }\n    .cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 7px; }\n    .card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto; align-items: baseline; column-gap: 8px; padding: 8px 12px; }\n    .card .subtle { grid-column: 1 / -1; }\n    .panel { padding: 14px; }\n    .notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 10px; }\n    th, td { padding: 7px 4px; }\n    thead { font-size: .68rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }\n  }\n  @page { size: letter; margin: .43in; }\n  @media print {\n    * { print-color-adjust: exact; -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; }\n    body { background: #fff; font-size: 10pt; }\n    .wrap { width: 100%; }\n    .skip, .print, .calculator { display: none !important; }\n    .mast { padding-inline: 14px; }\n    .mast-bar { min-height: 29px; }\n    .hero { padding-block: 11px 13px; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 14px; }\n    h1 { font-size: 32pt; }\n    h2 { font-size: 16pt; }\n    .hero-copy { margin-top: 5px; }\n    .rule dt, .rule dd { padding-block: 2px; font-size: 8pt; }\n    main { padding-block: 9px 0; }\n    .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 6px; margin-bottom: 9px; }\n    .card { display: block; padding: 5px 9px; }\n    .card .stat { font-size: 20pt; }\n    .subtle { font-size: 8pt; }\n    .workbench { display: block; }\n    .panel { padding: 9px 11px; break-inside: avoid; }\n    .legend { margin-block: 5px 9px; }\n    .plot { grid-template-rows: 104px auto; }\n    .chart-note { margin-top: 7px; padding: 4px 7px; }\n    .history { margin-top: 8px; }\n    .table-wrap { margin-top: 5px; overflow: visible; }\n    th, td { padding: 3px 7px; }\n    th, td, .over-cell small { font-size: 8pt; }\n    .over-cell small { display: inline; margin-left: 4px; }\n    .notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; margin-top: 8px; gap: 14px; }\n    .notes p, .notes h3 { font-size: 8pt; }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to comparison</a>\n<header class=\"mast\">\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <div class=\"mast-bar\">\n      <div class=\"brand eyebrow\"><span class=\"knob\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>Cabinet knob production</div>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"print\" id=\"print-button\">Print comparison</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"hero\">\n      <div>\n        <h1>Weekly batch planner</h1>\n        <p class=\"hero-copy\">Compare Friday-only shipping with Wednesday and Friday shipping using six weeks of fictional orders.</p>\n      </div>\n      <section class=\"rule\" aria-labelledby=\"rule-heading\">\n        <h2 id=\"rule-heading\">Suggested scheduling rule</h2>\n        <dl>\n          <dt>1–55 pieces</dt><dd>Run twice if there are orders ready for Wednesday. Otherwise run once.</dd>\n          <dt>56–61 pieces</dt><dd>Run once and ship Friday.</dd>\n          <dt>62+ pieces</dt><dd>Arrange extra time or carry work forward.</dd>\n        </dl>\n      </section>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</header>\n<main class=\"wrap\" id=\"main\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n  <div class=\"cards\" aria-label=\"Six-week comparison\">\n    <section class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Average weekly labor</h2>\n      <p class=\"stat\"><span id=\"avg-once\">203</span> / <span id=\"avg-twice\">228</span> <small>min</small></p>\n      <p class=\"subtle\">One run / two runs</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Orders shipped earlier</h2>\n      <p class=\"stat\"><span id=\"early-count\">39 of 66</span> <small>orders</small></p>\n      <p class=\"subtle\"><span id=\"early-percent\">59.1%</span> could move from Friday to Wednesday</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"card\">\n      <h2>Weeks within allowance</h2>\n      <p class=\"stat\"><span id=\"weeks-fit\">5 of 6</span> <small>each</small></p>\n      <p class=\"subtle\">270 labor minutes available per week</p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"workbench\">\n    <section class=\"panel\" aria-labelledby=\"chart-heading\">\n      <h2 id=\"chart-heading\">Labor against capacity</h2>\n      <p class=\"subtle\">The second setup adds 25 minutes every week.</p>\n      <figure aria-labelledby=\"chart-heading\" aria-describedby=\"chart-note\">\n        <div aria-hidden=\"true\">\n          <div class=\"legend\">\n            <span><b></b>One run</span>\n            <span><b class=\"second\"></b>Two runs</span>\n            <span><b class=\"limit\"></b>270 min allowance</span>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"plot\">\n            <div class=\"ticks\">\n              <span class=\"limit-tick\" style=\"--y:84.375%\">270</span>\n              <span style=\"--y:56.25%\">180</span>\n              <span style=\"--y:28.125%\">90</span>\n              <span style=\"--y:0%\">0</span>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bars\" id=\"chart-bars\"></div>\n            <div class=\"x-labels\" id=\"chart-labels\"></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <figcaption class=\"chart-note\" id=\"chart-note\"><strong>Week 4 · 62 pieces.</strong> One run is 3 min over. Two runs are 28 min over.</figcaption>\n      </figure>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"panel calculator\" aria-labelledby=\"calc-heading\">\n      <h2 id=\"calc-heading\">Plan a week</h2>\n      <p class=\"subtle\" id=\"calc-help\">Start with Week 6. Change the counts to check another week.</p>\n      <form id=\"calculator\" aria-describedby=\"calc-help\">\n        <div class=\"inputs\">\n          <label for=\"pieces\">Total pieces<input id=\"pieces\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\" required value=\"53\" inputmode=\"numeric\" aria-describedby=\"calc-error\"></label>\n          <label for=\"orders\">Total orders<input id=\"orders\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\" required value=\"13\" inputmode=\"numeric\" aria-describedby=\"calc-error\"></label>\n          <label for=\"eligible\">By Wed noon<input id=\"eligible\" type=\"number\" min=\"0\" step=\"1\" required value=\"7\" inputmode=\"numeric\" aria-describedby=\"calc-error\"></label>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"error\" id=\"calc-error\" role=\"status\" hidden></p>\n        <div id=\"calc-output\" aria-live=\"polite\" aria-atomic=\"true\">\n          <dl class=\"result-card\">\n            <div class=\"result\"><dt>One run</dt><dd><span class=\"time\" id=\"one-time\"></span><span id=\"one-margin\"></span></dd><dd id=\"one-ship\"></dd></div>\n            <div class=\"result\"><dt>Two runs</dt><dd><span class=\"time\" id=\"two-time\"></span><span id=\"two-margin\"></span></dd><dd id=\"two-ship\"></dd></div>\n          </dl>\n          <p class=\"scenario-summary\" id=\"scenario-summary\"></p>\n        </div>\n      </form>\n      <noscript><p class=\"error\">Enable JavaScript to use the calculator and render the weekly comparison.</p></noscript>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n  <section class=\"panel history\" aria-labelledby=\"history-heading\">\n    <h2 id=\"history-heading\">Six-week order record</h2>\n    <p class=\"subtle\" id=\"history-help\">“Earlier orders” counts orders that would move from Friday to Wednesday under two runs.</p>\n    <div class=\"table-wrap\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"history-heading\">\n      <table aria-describedby=\"history-help\">\n        <thead>\n          <tr>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Week</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Orders</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Pieces</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">One run<br>(min)</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Two runs<br>(min)</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Earlier<br>orders</th>\n            <th scope=\"col\">Friday orders<br>(two runs)</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody id=\"weeks\"></tbody>\n        <tfoot id=\"totals\"></tfoot>\n      </table>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"notes\">\n      <div>\n        <h3>Labor assumptions</h3>\n        <p>Labor = 4 minutes per piece + 25 minutes per scheduled run. Compare each week with 270 minutes. Spare time in other weeks cannot cover an overage within the same week.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div>\n        <h3>Shipping assumptions</h3>\n        <p>One run sends all orders Friday and moves zero earlier. Two runs assign orders received through Wednesday noon to Wednesday and the rest to Friday. Earlier orders include 10 in the over-capacity week and assume all scheduled work is completed. Midweek piece counts and labor availability are unknown, so confirm Wednesday readiness before committing.</p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n</main>\n<script>\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  const allowance = 270;\n  const setupMinutes = 25;\n  const pieceMinutes = 4;\n  const maxLaborChart = 320;\n  const weeks = [\n    { orders: 9, pieces: 35, eligible: 5 },\n    { orders: 12, pieces: 48, eligible: 8 },\n    { orders: 7, pieces: 28, eligible: 3 },\n    { orders: 15, pieces: 62, eligible: 10 },\n    { orders: 10, pieces: 41, eligible: 6 },\n    { orders: 13, pieces: 53, eligible: 7 }\n  ];\n  const get = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\n  const format = new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\");\n  const count = (value) => format.format(value);\n\n  function estimate({ orders, pieces, eligible }) {\n    const once = pieceMinutes * pieces + setupMinutes;\n    return { orders, pieces, eligible, once, twice: once + setupMinutes, friday: orders - eligible };\n  }\n\n  function renderHistory() {\n    const results = weeks.map(estimate);\n    const totals = { orders: 0, pieces: 0, once: 0, twice: 0, eligible: 0, friday: 0 };\n    const columns = Object.keys(totals);\n    for (const [index, week] of results.entries()) {\n      const row = document.createElement(\"tr\");\n      row.innerHTML = `<th scope=\"row\">${index + 1}</th>`;\n      for (const field of columns) {\n        totals[field] += week[field];\n        const cell = row.insertCell();\n        cell.textContent = count(week[field]);\n        if ((field === \"once\" || field === \"twice\") && week[field] > allowance) {\n          cell.classList.add(\"over-cell\");\n          const overage = document.createElement(\"small\");\n          overage.textContent = `${week[field] - allowance} over`;\n          cell.append(\" \", overage);\n        }\n      }\n      row.classList.toggle(\"over-row\", week.twice > allowance);\n      get(\"weeks\").append(row);\n\n      const pair = document.createElement(\"div\");\n      pair.className = \"pair\";\n      for (const labor of [week.once, week.twice]) {\n        const bar = document.createElement(\"span\");\n        bar.className = \"bar\";\n        bar.style.setProperty(\"--height\", `${labor / maxLaborChart * 100}%`);\n        pair.append(bar);\n      }\n      get(\"chart-bars\").append(pair);\n      const label = document.createElement(\"span\");\n      label.textContent = `W${index + 1}`;\n      get(\"chart-labels\").append(label);\n    }\n\n    get(\"totals\").innerHTML = `<tr><th scope=\"row\">Total</th>${columns.map((field) => `<td>${count(totals[field])}</td>`).join(\"\")}</tr>`;\n    get(\"avg-once\").textContent = count(totals.once / weeks.length);\n    get(\"avg-twice\").textContent = count(totals.twice / weeks.length);\n    get(\"early-count\").textContent = `${count(totals.eligible)} of ${count(totals.orders)}`;\n    get(\"early-percent\").textContent = `${(totals.eligible / totals.orders * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;\n    const fitsOnce = results.filter((week) => week.once <= allowance).length;\n    const fitsTwice = results.filter((week) => week.twice <= allowance).length;\n    get(\"weeks-fit\").textContent = fitsOnce === fitsTwice\n      ? `${fitsOnce} of ${weeks.length}`\n      : `${fitsOnce} / ${fitsTwice}`;\n  }\n\n  const fields = [get(\"pieces\"), get(\"orders\"), get(\"eligible\")];\n  const [piecesInput, ordersInput, eligibleInput] = fields;\n\n  function updateCalculator() {\n    const values = fields.map((field) => field.value === \"\" ? NaN : Number(field.value));\n    const [pieces, orders, eligible] = values;\n    const error = get(\"calc-error\");\n    const output = get(\"calc-output\");\n    let invalidFields = fields.filter((field, index) =>\n      !Number.isSafeInteger(values[index]) || values[index] < 0\n    );\n    let message = \"Enter whole, nonnegative counts in all three fields.\";\n\n    if (!invalidFields.length) {\n      if (eligible > orders) {\n        invalidFields = [eligibleInput];\n        message = \"Orders by Wednesday noon must be at most the total orders.\";\n      } else if (pieces < orders || (orders === 0 && pieces > 0)) {\n        invalidFields = [piecesInput, ordersInput];\n        message = \"Each order needs at least one piece. When there are zero orders, enter zero pieces.\";\n      } else if (!Number.isSafeInteger(pieceMinutes * pieces + 2 * setupMinutes)) {\n        invalidFields = [piecesInput];\n        message = \"Enter a smaller piece count.\";\n      }\n    }\n\n    for (const field of fields) {\n      field.setAttribute(\"aria-invalid\", String(invalidFields.includes(field)));\n    }\n    output.hidden = invalidFields.length > 0;\n    error.hidden = !output.hidden;\n    error.textContent = output.hidden ? message : \"\";\n    if (output.hidden) return;\n\n    const planned = estimate({ orders, pieces, eligible });\n    for (const [prefix, labor] of [[\"one\", planned.once], [\"two\", planned.twice]]) {\n      const remaining = allowance - labor;\n      const margin = get(`${prefix}-margin`);\n      get(`${prefix}-time`).textContent = `${count(labor)} min`;\n      margin.textContent = remaining < 0 ? `${count(-remaining)} min over` : remaining === 0 ? \"At allowance\" : `${count(remaining)} min spare`;\n      margin.classList.toggle(\"over\", remaining < 0);\n    }\n    get(\"one-ship\").textContent = `Fri: ${count(orders)}`;\n    get(\"two-ship\").textContent = `Wed: ${count(eligible)} · Fri: ${count(planned.friday)}`;\n\n    const summary = get(\"scenario-summary\");\n    summary.classList.toggle(\"exception\", planned.once > allowance);\n    if (orders === 0) {\n      summary.textContent = \"Skip production. The estimates above include setup only if a run is scheduled.\";\n    } else if (planned.once > allowance) {\n      summary.textContent = \"Both schedules exceed 270 minutes. Add labor time or move work before promising shipment.\";\n    } else if (planned.twice > allowance) {\n      summary.textContent = \"Run once and ship Friday. A second setup would exceed the weekly allowance.\";\n    } else if (eligible === 0) {\n      summary.textContent = \"Run once. The second setup would move zero orders to Wednesday.\";\n    } else {\n      const orderText = eligible === 1 ? \"1 order\" : `${count(eligible)} orders`;\n      summary.textContent = `Run twice if ready. ${orderText} could ship Wednesday instead of Friday.`;\n    }\n  }\n\n  renderHistory();\n  updateCalculator();\n  get(\"calculator\").addEventListener(\"input\", updateCalculator);\n  get(\"calculator\").addEventListener(\"submit\", (event) => event.preventDefault());\n  get(\"print-button\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => window.print());\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}],"download":"data/release/assets/a2e824a01f1e15c3a5e96630857b47e505fcb25a999ccaef0415b820eecd4520.zip"}}}
